  "notes": "A practical word frequently seen on food packaging, in recipes, and in cooking instructions. The noun form {加熱|かねつ} is used as a modifier.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {加熱|かねつ}{調理|ちょうり}: cooking by heating\n- {加熱|かねつ}{処理|しょり}: heat treatment\n- {加熱|かねつ}{殺菌|さっきん}: heat sterilization\n- {加熱|かねつ}{式|しき}タバコ: heated tobacco product\n- {加熱|かねつ}{時間|じかん}: heating time\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {温|あたた}める: to warm up — everyday word, gentler heating\n- {加熱|かねつ}する: to heat — more technical, implies deliberate application of heat for a purpose\n- {焼|や}く: to burn, to grill — involves direct fire or high heat for cooking",
